unmet: the same trial on a pristine card, judged by the board's expectation:
unmet: boot: slot B -- a trial (committed is A); the watchdog holds the rollback until the boot is judged
unmet: boot: watchdog -- off by the boot line (the emulator resets on arming); a trial cannot roll back by hardware here
unmet: boot: identity -- ed25519, custody a file at /data/device.key -- created on this device, fingerprint KEY3
unmet: boot: health -- kds every 5s, poste every 5s; a world that stops refreshing stops the watchdog
unmet: boot: start kds -- pid N -- /stzr /app/kds.luau
unmet: kds: the kitchen display world is up on the Makeen box (aarch64, stzr under PID 1)
unmet: kds: read /etc/machine -- 8 declarations rode in the image
unmet: kds: serving -- signalling /run/kds.ready
unmet: boot: kds -- ready (/run/kds.ready)
unmet: boot: start poste -- pid N -- /stzr /app/poste.luau
unmet: poste: the counter world is up on the Makeen box, after kds
unmet: poste: /data is the box's persistent partition, mounted by PID 1 before any world spoke
unmet: poste: serving -- signalling /run/poste.ready
unmet: boot: poste -- ready (/run/poste.ready)
unmet: boot: judge -- the boot differs from its expectation (/etc/expected): 2 line(s) expected and not said, 2 said and not expected
unmet: boot: judge -- expected, not said: network lan -- eth0 up 192.168.10.1/24
unmet: boot: judge -- expected, not said: watchdog armed (/dev/watchdog)
unmet: boot: judge -- said, not expected: network lan -- eth0: no such interface (NODEV)
unmet: boot: judge -- said, not expected: watchdog -- off by the boot line (the emulator resets on arming); a trial cannot roll back by hardware here
unmet: boot: slot B -- held: every service is ready but the boot is not the one expected; not committed, the watchdog is no longer fed -- the next boot is A
unmet: boot: --halt-on-verdict: every service is ready and the boot is judged; the court ends what a real init never would
unmet: boot: init halts the machine -- reboot(RESTART)
unmet: reboot: Restarting system
